      "transcript_text": "No, I haven't fallen. I'm steady enough, thanks.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:31",
      "end_timestamp": "01:36",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Last of the nerve questions. Any trouble with your bladder or bowels?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:38",
      "end_timestamp": "01:46",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, nothing like that.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:48",
      "end_timestamp": "01:52",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good, those are the ones I worry about most. Do you have any other health conditions?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:53",
      "end_timestamp": "02:03",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Type 2 diabetes. Diet only so far, the GP keeps an eye on it.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:05",
      "end_timestamp": "02:13",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And does anybody else in the family have diabetes?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:16",
      "end_timestamp": "02:22",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "My father did. He had diabetes for years before he passed.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:22",
      "end_timestamp": "02:29",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Thanks for telling me. Do you smoke?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:31",
      "end_timestamp": "02:36",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "About ten cigarettes a day. I know, I know.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:37",
      "end_timestamp": "02:43",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'm not going to nag, your daughter has that covered. What about alcohol?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:46",
      "end_timestamp": "02:54",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "A couple of pints on a Saturday at the club. That's my lot.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:55",
      "end_timestamp": "03:02",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Any allergies to medicines or anything else?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:20",
      "end_timestamp": "03:24",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "None that I know of.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:26",
      "end_timestamp": "03:30",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Not at all. Blood pressure is 136 over 84, and your pulse is 72.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:08",
      "end_timestamp": "04:16",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Thank you. The feeling is reduced in the toes of your left foot, compared with the right.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:59",
      "end_timestamp": "05:07",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Let me explain it plainly. Nerves are like electrical cables, and years of high sugar can wear away the insulation, so the signal gets fuzzy. It looks like early nerve damage from the diabetes.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:15",
      "end_timestamp": "05:31",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It can be slowed down a lot. Step one is bloods. I'd like to order blood tests, for your sugar control and your vitamin B12, since a low B12 can do something similar.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:38",
      "end_timestamp": "05:58",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "The nurse can take them on your way out. Then I'd like to see you in two weeks, to go through the results together.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:03",
      "end_timestamp": "06:16",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]",
        "follow_up[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Please do. And look after those feet in the meantime. Check them every evening, and wear slippers indoors.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:26",
      "end_timestamp": "06:36",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    }
